Starscourge Radahn, the Red Lion General, wanted nothing more than an honorable death. He dueled Malenia, Blade of Miquella at the Battle of Aeonia toward the end of the Shattering. To match Radahn's measure, Malenia snapped Miquella's Needle to unleash her first-ever Scarlet Aeonia bloom. Though Radahn survived the encounter, he was afflicted with the incurable scarlet rot. Over time, the rot ate away at him until he lost his wits and degenerated into a feral beast. Still alive, the Demigod never received his warrior's end.

During the Shattering, Witch-Hunter Jerren served General Radahn in his Redmane army. He was duty-bound to maintain Redmane Castle as long as Radahn lived. He organized the Radahn Festival to ensure his master received a noble warrior's death. When the stars aligned, champions from across the Lands Between gathered at Redmane Castle Plaza to challenge Radahn. They came seeking glory and Radahn's Great Rune. They reveled and made merry before departing through the north gate to the Wailing Dunes, where Starscourge Radahn devoured their soon corpses and howled at the sky.
